  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001, rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000) has been completed, yielding a low baseline of ~48.5% accuracy. This tells us little about whether the image modality carries any useful signal for this task. Uncertainty: The most consequential architectural question is whether image features contribute meaningfully at all—if they do not, ~28 multimodal/image-only configurations can be eliminated from consideration. What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest possible probe of image-modality signal, using a standard, well-established backbone (ResNet-50) and matching the singleprofile setting of the RNA baseline for a fair unimodal comparison. Why it is the best next experiment: Under a tight budget, resolving the binary question 'does image modality help?' has the highest information value because it branches the entire remaining search space. If image accuracy is comparable to or below the RNA baseline, I can focus subsequent experiments on RNA encoder and profile improvements. If it is substantially higher, I can prioritize multimodal fusion strategies. No other single experiment would reduce uncertainty about this many downstream decisions."
}

